{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r2s0.yaml\nrg -n \\\"hypothesis.schema|jsonschema.*hypothesis|validate.*hypothesis\\\" tools schemas Makefile | head -80\ngit status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r2s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Qualify load-use hazards by actual source operands\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The load-use detector compares a load destination against both raw rs1 and\n  rs2 bitfields of the following instruction. Those fields are not both source\n  registers for many RV32 formats: OP-IMM, loads, and JALR do not read rs2,\n  while LUI, AUIPC, and JAL read neither field. Coincidental matches therefore\n  inject unnecessary bubbles into CoreMark without protecting any dependency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Derive compact uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 qualifiers from the following\n  instruction's opcode and gate each load-destination comparison with the\n  corresponding qualifier. Preserve the existing one-cycle bubble for every\n  true dependency, including store data and branch operands, while allowing\n  false matches in immediate and upper-immediate encodings to proceed. This\n  removes avoidable cycles with only shallow opcode-decode logic off the main\n  execute datapath, so CoreMark iterations per cycle should improve with\n  negligible Fmax or area cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 1\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Classify which source operands the IF/ID opcode actually reads and gate the rs1 and rs2 load-use comparisons accordingly, while retaining all existing redirect, divider, and bus-stall priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Pass the complete IF/ID instruction into the hazard unit so source-use qualification is based on the pending instruction without changing the nret=1 interface or retirement behavior.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed adjacent-load cases proving true OP, OP-IMM, store-data, and branch dependencies still stall and false matches embedded in unused immediate, LUI, AUIPC, and JAL fields do not create bubbles.\"\ntools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:220:        emit_verilog, offlimits_changes, _read_notes, validate_hypothesis,\ntools/tournament.py:261:        hyp = validate_hypothesis(hyp_path)\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:444:def validate_hypothesis(hyp_path: str) -> dict:\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:94:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:282:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
