igh-half result on completion. Unlike the prior shared-product\n  experiment, this adds no correction subtractors or signedness muxing to the\n  common MUL/ALU result path. CoreMark cycles should remain essentially\n  unchanged because multiply-high instructions are absent or extremely rare,\n  while removing two wide combinational multipliers should improve placement\n  freedom and median Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Retain only the single-cycle low-half unsigned MUL product and remove real combinational MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU products, while preserving the existing ALTOPS definitions.\"\n  - file: rtl/mulh_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add one shared iterative multiply-high unit for signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned variants with exact RV32M sign handling and a shallow bounded-latency ALTOPS handshake.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Launch multiply-high operations once with post-forwarded operands, retain their complete payload, merge their busy/completion protocol with the divider interlock, and advance exactly one result despite dmem backpressure.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed multiply-high dependencies, back-to-back long operations, randomized bus stalls, and RVFI checks proving correct results, progress, and single retirement.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Extend signed-boundary and randomized MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU vectors to guard exact high-half arithmetic after the implementation moves out of the combinational ALU.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
