003-r7s2.log\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r8s2.log\ncores/bench/experiments/run_summary.json\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed1/nextpnr.log\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed1/pnr.json\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed2/nextpnr.log\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed2/pnr.json\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed3/nextpnr.log\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed3/pnr.json\ncores/bench/generated/synth.json\nhyp-20260711-001-r5s0\tReplace the generic dmem_rdata shift with width-specific direct lane selects:\\na four-way 8-bit mux for byte loads, a two-way 16-bit mux for aligned\\nhalfword loads, and an unmodified word path. Perform sign or zero extension\\nonly after the narrow mux, and express store masks with explicit address\\ncases rather than variable shifts. This preserves every load value, memory\\nmask, misalignment trap, bypass qualification, and pipeline cycle while\\nreducing the combinational depth and switched routing between memory and EX,\\nso median Fmax should improve without an IPC penalty.\\n\t\nhyp-20260711-001-r6s0\tIntroduce stage-specific post-EX and post-MEM control payloads and retain only\\nthe bits consumed downstream: memory access controls in EX/MEM, and writeback\\nplus trap controls in MEM/WB. Remove the unused registered branch-taken and\\nbranch-target metadata while leaving the existing dedicated target adders and\\nredirect datapath unchanged. Unlike the earlier experiment that combined\\nmetadata pruning with a slower shared control-flow adder, this isolates the\\nregister and routing reduction. CoreMark cycles should remain identical while\\nthe smaller pipeline registers and reduced control fanout modestly improve\\nplacement and median Fmax.\\n\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
