{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r5s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\\\") | \\\"ID: \\\"+.id+\\\"\\\\nTITLE: \\\"+.title+\\\"\\\\nHYP: \\\"+(.hypothesis.hypothesis//\\\"\\\")+\\\"\\\\nCHANGES: \\\"+((.changes//[])|tostring)+\\\"\\\\nNOTES: \\\"+(.implementation_notes//\\\"\\\")+\\\"\\\\n\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r5s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\\\") | \\\"ID: \\\"+.id+\\\"\\\\nTITLE: \\\"+.title+\\\"\\\\nHYP: \\\"+(.hypothesis.hypothesis//\\\"\\\")+\\\"\\\\nCHANGES: \\\"+((.changes//[])|tostring)+\\\"\\\\nNOTES: \\\"+(.implementation_notes//\\\"\\\")+\\\"\\\\n\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"ID: hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\nTITLE: Collapse redundant execute-stage target adders\nHYP: Select PC and the decoded immediate as the main ALU operands for conditional branches\nand direct JAL, and select forwarded rs1 and the immediate for JALR, allowing the ALU's\nexisting ADD result to serve as the sole control-flow target sum. Apply JALR bit-zero\nclearing after that shared result, while leaving the separate comparators, redirect\nrules, misalignment traps, PC-plus-four link value, and dmem-stall suppression intact.\nRemove the dead branch_taken and branch_target fields from EX/MEM so they no longer\nconsume flops or routing. Eliminating redundant adders and payload should improve\nmedian FPGA Fmax with no CoreMark cycle penalty and no change to architectural state.\n\nCHANGES: [{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Route branch, JAL, and JALR target arithmetic through the existing ALU ADD path; preserve forwarding, JALR alignment, redirect gating, traps, link writes, divider interlocks, and RVFI pc_wdata behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from ex_mem_t to reduce EX/MEM register width and downstream routing.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Update the EX/MEM payload usage annotations after pruning dead branch metadata, without changing memory or RVFI behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add directed taken and not-taken branches plus JAL and forwarded JALR cases, including misaligned targets and bus stalls, to verify shared target arithmetic and exact RVFI next PCs.\"}]\nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r5s0\nTITLE: Replace load barrel shift with lane muxes\nHYP: Replace the generic dmem_rdata shift with width-specific direct lane selects:\na four-way 8-bit mux for byte loads, a two-way 16-bit mux for aligned\nhalfword loads, and an unmodified word path. Perform sign or zero extension\nonly after the narrow mux, and express store masks with explicit address\ncases rather than variable shifts. This preserves every load value, memory\nmask, misalignment trap, bypass qualification, and pipeline cycle while\nreducing the combinational depth and switched routing between memory and EX,\nso median Fmax should improve without an IPC penalty.\n\nCHANGES: [{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the generic 32-bit load shift and variable store-mask shift with narrow explicit byte/halfword lane muxes and address-case masks, preserving alignment traps, RVFI fields, and the same-cycle load bypass.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add directed LB/LBU cases at every byte offset and LH/LHU cases at both aligned halfword offsets, including adjacent dependent consumers and dmem stalls, to verify lane selection, extension, bypass timing, and RVFI masks.\"}]\nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\nTITLE: Narrow post-execute pipeline metadata\nHYP: Introduce stage-specific post-EX and post-MEM control payloads and retain only\nthe bits consumed downstream: memory access controls in EX/MEM, and writeback\nplus trap controls in MEM/WB. Remove the unused registered branch-taken and\nbranch-target metadata while leaving the existing dedicated target adders and\nredirect datapath unchanged. Unlike the earlier experiment that combined\nmetadata pruning with a slower shared control-flow adder, this isolates the\nregister and routing reduction. CoreMark cycles should remain identical while\nthe smaller pipeline registers and reduced control fanout modestly improve\nplacement and median Fmax.\n\nCHANGES: [{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Define narrow EX/MEM and MEM/WB control payloads, use them in the corresponding bundles, and remove downstream-unused branch_taken and branch_target fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Pack only memory, writeback, and trap controls into EX/MEM for normal and divider-completion paths while preserving all arithmetic, redirect, alignment, stall, and RVFI behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM controls and emit only writeback and trap controls into MEM/WB, preserving memory masks, load bypass, misalignment traps, and held-WB semantics.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update hazard and forwarding control references for the narrowed bundles without changing the nret=1 interface, bus handshakes, or retirement ordering.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/wb_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Use the narrowed MEM/WB writeback controls with unchanged register-file write qualification and result selection.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add directed ALU, load/store, illegal-instruction, branch/jump, divider, dependency, and randomized bus-stall coverage to prove metadata pruning is cycle- and RVFI-transparent.\"}]\nNOTES: \n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
