{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r5s1.yaml')\nprint(p.read_text())\ntry:\n import yaml\n d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\n assert d['id']=='hyp-20260711-002-r5s1'\n assert d['category']=='structural'\n assert isinstance(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'], int)\n assert all(x['file'].startswith(('rtl/','test/test_')) for x in d['changes'])\n print('YAML parse and required-field checks: PASS')\nexcept Exception as e:\n print(f'VALIDATION FAILED: {e}')\n raise\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-002-r5s1\ntitle: \"Retime PC-relative targets ahead of execute\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The frequent conditional branches in CoreMark currently place a 32-bit\n  PC-plus-immediate adder in the EX-to-fetch redirect cone. Prior predictor\n  attempts show that target arithmetic and selection on a fetch-PC path are\n  particularly expensive on this FPGA, while sharing more logic into the main\n  EX adder also regressed. The PC and immediate are already available one stage\n  earlier, so this work need not remain in the redirect stage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute PC-relative targets for BRANCH and JAL in decode and register the\n  result in ID/EX. EX will use that registered target for branch comparison,\n  redirect, misalignment checking, RVFI pc_wdata, and captured metadata, while\n  retaining the existing forwarded rs1-plus-immediate path for JALR. This\n  retimes the dedicated 32-bit target adder across the ID/EX boundary and\n  shortens the common branch redirect path without changing branch penalties,\n  retirement timing, prediction state, or the nret=1 interface. The decode\n  target computation is independent of regfile data, so it should trade a\n  relatively uncongested ID cone for higher median Fmax on the control-critical\n  EX-to-PC feedback path with no CoreMark cycle increase.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a registered PC-relative target field to the ID/EX payload, without changing any architectural or RVFI-visible field.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute PC plus the decoded B/J immediate and latch it into ID/EX only when the stage advances, preserving reset, flush, and stall semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered target for conditional branches and JAL in redirect, alignment, pc_next, and saved metadata paths; keep forwarded operand addition for JALR and all existing divider/backpressure behavior.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed forward/backward branch and JAL cases across randomized stalls, including misaligned targets, to verify redirects, traps, RVFI pc_wdata, and one-copy retirement after the retiming.\"\n\nYAML parse and required-field checks: PASS\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
