{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r7s1.yaml && sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r7s1.yaml\nruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; x=YAML.safe_load_file(ARGV[0]); abort unless x[\\\"id\\\"]==\\\"hyp-20260711-002-r7s1\\\" && x[\\\"category\\\"]==\\\"structural\\\" && x.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer) && %w[low medium high].include?(x.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"confidence\\\")) && x[\\\"changes\\\"].all?{|c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\"'^(rtl/[''^.].*|test/test_[''^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\"'$})}; puts \"YAML structure and paths valid\"'\"' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r7s1.yaml\ngit status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r7s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-002-r7s1\ntitle: \"Cold-path high-half multiply operations\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The common execute path still contains three separately described 64-bit\n  products for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU. CoreMark needs ordinary low-half\n  MUL but is not expected to execute the three high-half variants inside the\n  timed region. The earlier attempt to algebraically share one combinational\n  product regressed because its sign-correction subtractors enlarged the same\n  one-cycle path; moving only the cold variants out of that path avoids that\n  correction cone while preserving common-case multiply throughput.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep RV32M MUL as the existing single-cycle low-half product, but implement\n  MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU in one shared iterative shift-add unit. On a high-half\n  multiply, EX captures the post-forwarding operands and complete instruction\n  payload, holds younger stages through the existing long-operation interlock,\n  emits bubbles while the unit runs, and advances the result exactly once.\n  Signedness is handled by operand normalization and final 64-bit sign restore,\n  with the architectural result taken from bits 63:32. This removes two cold\n  64-bit multiplier structures and their result-selection routing from the\n  ordinary ALU while leaving CoreMark's single-cycle MUL latency and cycle count\n  unchanged, so reduced DSP/LUT routing pressure should raise median Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mulh_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a shared iterative 32-step shift-add engine for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU with signed operand normalization, 64-bit sign restoration, a one-shot start/busy/done protocol, and a shallow RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS path.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Retain only the single-cycle low-half MUL product in the normal ALU and remove combinational MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU products, while preserving all ALTOPS opcode results.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Route high-half multiply instructions through the new unit, capture forwarded operands and RVFI payload at launch, reuse the long-operation hold discipline, and emit one completed EX/MEM result across dmem backpressure without affecting ordinary MUL or DIV/REM.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Generalize the existing EX long-operation interlock, if needed, so high-half multiply and divide completion share the same redirect and bus-stall priorities without replaying or dropping instructions.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the generalized long-operation busy path while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface, single retirement channel, and strict RVFI order.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Keep direct single-cycle MUL coverage and verify that high-half operations no longer depend on combinational ALU outputs.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add signed and unsigned high-half multiply dependencies, back-to-back long operations, and randomized imem/dmem stall cases checking exact results, bounded progress, single retirement, and RVFI operand data.\"\n-e:1:in `<main>': undefined method `safe_load_file' for Psych:Module (NoMethodError)\nDid you mean?  safe_load\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
