ription\": \"Add repeated-loop, loop-exit, entry-replacement, stale-target, and randomized bus-stall tests checking wrong-path suppression, RVFI PCs, order, and forward progress.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 212.65, \"delta_pct\": -48.49, \"vs_baseline\": -24.81, \"fmax_mhz\": 87.38, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4109157, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5848, \"ff\": 2297, \"seeds\": [85.03, 87.38, 97.1], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T22:39:58.289519Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r7s2 (regression, -48.49%): Even a single fully registered loop-target entry leaves a 32-bit exact-PC compare and predicted-target mux in the fetch-PC recurrence, so eliminating predecode, target arithmetic, and table indexing is insufficient unless prediction lookup is also decoupled from next-PC selection.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
