{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; d=YAML.safe_load(File.read(ARGV[0])); abort \\\"bad id\\\" unless d[\\\"id\\\"]==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r1s2\\\"; abort \\\"bad category\\\" unless d[\\\"category\\\"]==\\\"predictor\\\"; abort \\\"bad impact\\\" unless d.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer); abort \\\"bad confidence\\\" unless %w[low medium high].include?(d.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"confidence\\\")); abort \\\"bad path\\\" unless d[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(/\\\\A(rtl\\\\/[\"'^.].*|test'\"\\\\/test_[\"'^'\"\\\\/]+\\\\.py)\\\\z/) }; puts \\\"YAML structure and paths valid\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r1s2.yaml\nsed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r1s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"YAML structure and paths valid\nid: hyp-20260711-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Tiny tagged BTB with direction counters\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Every taken branch or jump is currently discovered in EX, after two younger\n  instructions have entered the front end and must be discarded. CoreMark has\n  frequent loop backedges and control-flow transfers, so this fixed redirect\n  penalty directly reduces iterations per cycle. A small BTB supplies an\n  already-computed target and therefore keeps target generation out of the\n  fetch critical path, which is important because fitness also scales with\n  FPGA Fmax and the design is close to its LUT target.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 16-entry direct-mapped tagged branch target buffer indexed by fetch PC,\n  with a 2-bit saturating direction counter per entry. Predict tagged JAL and\n  JALR entries taken unconditionally and conditional branches from the counter;\n  update target, type, and counter only when a valid control-flow instruction\n  actually advances through EX. Carry the predicted next PC with the\n  instruction and recover in EX whenever resolved next PC differs, covering\n  both taken misses and false-taken predictions. This should remove most loop\n  backedge penalties and learn stable jump targets while keeping predictor\n  state and combinational lookup small enough to preserve Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add the 16-entry tagged BTB, control-flow type bits, 2-bit counters, lookup, and accepted-EX update logic.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry predicted-next-PC metadata and prediction validity through the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use a valid BTB prediction as the fetch next PC and emit the prediction metadata with the fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata into ID/EX without changing decoder legality behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the prediction against the resolved architectural next PC, recover on either prediction direction error, and expose predictor training information only when EX advances.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate and connect the predictor, prediction metadata, recovery path, and stall-qualified training interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat any predictor recovery as a redirect that flushes younger wrong-path work while preserving existing stall priorities.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
