{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r2s2.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; require \\\"json\\\"; d=YAML.safe_load(File.read(ARGV[0])); abort \\\"bad id\\\" unless d[\\\"id\\\"]==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r2s2\\\"; abort \\\"bad category\\\" unless d[\\\"category\\\"]==\\\"predictor\\\"; abort \\\"bad impact\\\" unless d.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer); abort \\\"bad paths\\\" unless d[\\\"changes\\\"].all?{|c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(/\\\\A(?:rtl\\\\/[\"'^'\"\\\\/]+\\\\.sv|test\\\\/test_[\"'^'\"\\\\/]+\\\\.py)\\\\z/)}; puts JSON.pretty_generate(d)' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r2s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r2s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Table-free backward-branch and JAL prediction\",\n  \"category\": \"predictor\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The prior tagged BTB reduced the CoreMark cycle count, showing that avoiding\\nEX-stage redirect bubbles has useful IPC value, but its indexed tag, counter,\\ntarget lookup, and fetch-PC mux reduced median Fmax enough to dominate the\\ngain. CoreMark loop backedges and direct calls can be predicted without any\\nlearned state or target storage because their direction and target immediate\\nare already present in the fetched instruction.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Add a table-free static predictor in fetch that predicts conditional branches\\ntaken only when their B-immediate is negative, predicts direct JAL instructions\\ntaken unconditionally, and predicts all other instructions sequentially.\\nForm the predicted target directly from the fetch PC and instruction immediate,\\nqualify prediction on io_imemReady, and carry only the predicted next PC through\\nID into EX. EX compares that value with the resolved architectural next PC and\\nredirects on either a false-taken or missed-taken prediction; JALR remains\\nresolved in EX. With no entries, tags, counters, target array, or update path,\\nthis should recover much of the observed loop/call cycle reduction while adding\\nonly immediate wiring, one target adder, and a small opcode/direction mux to the\\nfetch path, greatly limiting the Fmax and LUT penalty that defeated the BTB.\\n\",\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 4,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a predicted-next-PC field to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so EX can verify the static fetch decision without any predictor table state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Decode only BRANCH and JAL opcodes from the ready fetched word, construct their immediates, predict backward conditional branches and all direct JALs taken, and select the corresponding next fetch PC while preserving redirect and stall priority.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Latch the predicted next PC alongside the instruction while leaving decoder legality and architectural operands unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Compute the resolved architectural next PC, redirect only when it differs from the carried prediction, and retain existing misalignment-trap, divider, RVFI pc_wdata, and memory-stall behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Wire the prediction-aware EX recovery signal through the existing redirect and flush path without changing the nret=1 top-level interface or retirement ordering.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed backward-branch, forward-branch, JAL, JALR, misprediction-recovery, and randomized bus-stall cases that check exact retirement order and architectural next PCs.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
