 the predictor, prediction metadata, recovery path, and stall-qualified training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat any predictor recovery as a redirect that flushes younger wrong-path work while preserving existing stall priorities.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 246.71, \"delta_pct\": -12.77, \"vs_baseline\": -12.77, \"fmax_mhz\": 104.46, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4234052, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12368, \"ff\": 2922, \"seeds\": [103.31, 104.46, 104.65], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T20:59:19.742035Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r1s2 (regression, -12.77%): Even a 16-entry tagged BTB leaves an indexed tag/counter/target read and taken mux on the fetch-PC feedback path, so its timing cost can outweigh CoreMark's saved EX redirect bubbles unless lookup is pipelined or decoupled.\"}\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Qualify load-use hazards by actual source operands\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector compares a load destination against both raw rs1 and\\nrs2 bitfields of the following instruction. Those fields are not both source\\nregisters for many RV32 formats: OP-IMM, loads, and JALR do not read rs2,\\nwhile LUI, AUIPC, and JAL read neither field. Coincidental matches therefore\\ninject unnecessary bubbles into CoreMark without protecting any dependency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use detector compares a load destination against both raw rs1 and\\nrs2 bitfields of the following instruction. Those fields are not both source\\nregisters for many RV32 formats: OP-IMM, loads, and JALR do not read rs2,\\nwhile LUI, AUIPC, and JAL read neither field. Coincidental matches therefore\\ninject unnecessary bubbles into CoreMark without protecting any dependency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Derive compact uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 qualifiers from the following\\ninstruction's opcode and gate each load-destination comparison with the\\ncorresponding qualifier. Preserve the existing one-cycle bubble for every\\ntrue dependency, including store data and branch operands, while allowing\\nfalse matches in immediate and upper-immediate encodings to proceed. This\\nremoves avoidable cycles with only shallow opcode-decode logic off the main\\nexecute datapath, so CoreMark iterations per cycle should improve with\\nnegligible Fmax or area cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which source operands the IF/ID opcode actually reads and gate the rs1 and rs2 load-use comparisons accordingly, while retaining all existing redirect, divider, and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the complete IF/ID instruction into the hazard unit so source-use qualification is based on the pending instruction without changing the nret=1 interface or retirement behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed adjacent-load cases proving true OP, OP-IMM, store-data, and branch dependencies still stall and false matches embedded in unused immediate, LUI, AUIPC, and JAL fields do not create bubbles.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify which source operands the IF/ID opcode actually reads and gate the rs1 and rs2 load-use comparisons accordingly, while retaining all existing redirect, divider, and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the complete IF/ID instruction into the hazard unit so source-use qualification is based on the pending instruction without changing the nret=1 interface or retirement behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test