{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r3s2.yaml && rg -n \\\"hypothesis.schema|yaml.safe_load|validate.*hypothesis\\\" tools schemas Makefile\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Tiny return-address stack for canonical returns\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The two broader predictors reduced control-flow bubbles but lost fitness because\n  BTB lookup or immediate target generation lengthened the fetch-PC feedback path.\n  CoreMark still pays the full EX-stage redirect penalty on every function return,\n  while a return target is already known when its call executes and can be retained\n  in a few registers without tags, counters, or a target adder at fetch.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a four-entry return-address stack that pushes PC+4 when a legal call writing\n  x1 advances through EX and pops when a canonical RET (JALR x0,x1,0) advances.\n  In fetch, recognize only that canonical RET and, when the stack is nonempty and\n  imem is ready, select the registered stack top as predicted next PC. Carry the\n  predicted next PC with the instruction and let EX redirect only if the resolved\n  architectural next PC differs, so stale, underflowed, or unusual JALR cases recover\n  normally. This targets frequent function returns while keeping the added feedback\n  path to a narrow instruction predecode and mux, avoiding the target adder and the\n  indexed tag/counter arrays that caused both earlier predictor regressions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/return_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a four-entry return-address stack with EX-accept-qualified call pushes and canonical-return pops, exposing only a registered top target and nonempty flag.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry predicted-next-PC metadata through IF/ID and ID/EX so return predictions can be verified in EX without changing architectural RVFI fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize canonical RET instructions, qualify prediction on imem readiness and stack validity, and select the precomputed stack-top target without an immediate adder or table lookup.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch return-prediction metadata alongside the instruction while preserving default-illegal decode and source operand reporting.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare carried predicted next PC with the resolved JALR next PC, recover on mismatch, and emit stall-qualified call/return events for precise stack updates.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate and connect the return predictor, prediction recovery, and update signals through the existing redirect/flush path without changing the nret=1 interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add nested-call, canonical-return, stack-underflow, noncanonical-JALR, misprediction-recovery, and randomized bus-stall tests checking exact retirement and RVFI next PCs.\"\ntools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:220:        emit_verilog, offlimits_changes, _read_notes, validate_hypothesis,\ntools/tournament.py:261:        hyp = validate_hypothesis(hyp_path)\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:94:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/agents/implement.py:170:        hypothesis = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:161:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:185:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:218:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:235:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/eval/formal.py:32:    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:282:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:338:        data = yaml.safe_load(raw)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:351:            data = yaml.safe_load(repaired)\ntools/test_core_yaml_update.py:24:    y = yaml.safe_load((core_dir / \"core.yaml\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:152:    y = yaml.safe_load(yaml_path.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:365:                    y = yaml.safe_load(candidate.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:444:def validate_hypothesis(hyp_path: str) -> dict:\ntools/orchestrator.py:446:        hyp = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/orchestrator.py:605:        y = yaml.safe_load((src / \"core.yaml\").read_text()) or {}\ntools/bench/runner.py:99:    cfg = yaml.safe_load(path.read_text())\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
